    "title": "North Powder water discoloration caused by hydrant flushing, public works clarifies - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Garrett Christensen ,\n15 hours ago NORTH POWDER – On Monday evening, some North Powder residents may have noticed brown water discoloration from their faucets. According to North Powder public works, this was the result of, predominantly, then ongoing hydrant flushing of the city’s water system, as well as a brief drop in pressure three weeks ago. Read full article",
